{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "m9_datm_clm",
  "description": "M9 subassembly: datm -> CLM atmospheric forcing (stage 2 of the EqESM project; milestone M9 - subassemblies across components, PLAN.md section 10). Couples the data atmosphere (CDEPS datm, GSWP3v1 datamode, cdeps_datm_gswp3.esm:Clmncep) to the CLM atmospheric-forcing import and downscaling (clm_atm_forcing.esm:ImportFields + Downscale) exactly as the CESM mediator hands the datm exports to the land in the I2000Clm60Sp reference case: every Sa_*/Faxa_* field the datm exports is imported by CLM without mediator-side alteration (the mediator only maps the fields by name; the datm -> land conversions of stage1/boundaries.md section 2.6 are all inside the components). The variable_map couplings below therefore implement the state_getimport mapping of lnd_import_export.F90:542-577 (Sa_z -> forc_hgt, Sa_topo -> forc_topo, Sa_u/Sa_v -> forc_u/forc_v, Sa_shum -> forc_q, Sa_ptem -> forc_th, Sa_pbot -> forc_pbot, Sa_tbot -> forc_t, Faxa_rainc..Faxa_snowl -> forc_rainc..forc_snowl, Faxa_lwdn -> forc_lwrad, Faxa_swvdr/swndr/swvdf/swndf -> forc_solad_vis/nir/solai_vis/nir), and the ImportFields -> Downscale wiring repeats the internal coupling of clm_atm_forcing.esm, because the CLI cannot mount a file's internal couplings by reference: mounting clm_atm_forcing.esm as a single model fails validation with the exact error 'Schema validation error: [toplevel_model_ref_unresolved] top-level model ref '../stage2/clm_atm_forcing.esm' resolves to 2 models; add a \"model\" selector to choose one (available: Downscale, ImportFields)' (probed under scratch/, 2026-11-06). The tests pin the coupled chain against the stage-1 dumps on the overlapping (cell, step) rows: CLM dump columns c = 1..5 at steps s = 1..12 (the South Pole row; the five traced cells are value-identical, so cell 1 pins all of them) are driven by the GSWP3v1 interpolated stream values of datm_gswp3_streams.csv at (step s - 1, cell 1) and asserted against the CLM column forcing of clm_bareground/clm_canopyflux (stage=ent rows, which carry the forc_rain/forc_snow inputs)/clm_surfrad at (step s, cell 1). The one-step offset is the CESM coupling sequence itself: the data atmosphere runs after the land within each coupling interval, so the land is forced by the atmosphere of the previous interval (verified: every forc_* dump value equals its one-step-earlier datm export bit-exact). The traced columns are non-glacier soil columns (needs_downscaling = 0) and repartition_rain_snow is active but degenerate at the pole (forc_t ~ 249 K below the nonglc all-snow ramp start, so frac_rain = 0 and all precipitation stays snow). Reference: stage1/cesm/components/clm/src/cpl/nuopc/lnd_import_export.F90, cpl/utils/lnd_import_export_utils.F90, main/atm2lndMod.F90; stage1/cesm/cime/cases/I2000Clm60Sp_clm_inst/run/lnd_in; stage1/dumps/cdeps/datm_gswp3_streams.csv, datm_gswp3_exports.csv, stage1/dumps/clm/clm_bareground.csv, clm_canopyflux.csv, clm_surfrad.csv.",
  "license": "MIT"
 },
 "models": {
  "Clmncep": {
   "ref": "./cdeps_datm_gswp3.esm",
   "model": "Clmncep"
  },
  "ImportFields": {
   "ref": "./clm_atm_forcing.esm",
   "model": "ImportFields"
  },
  "Downscale": {
   "ref": "./clm_atm_forcing.esm",
   "model": "Downscale"
  },
  "M9": {
   "variables": {},
   "equations": [],
   "tests": [
     {
      "id": "step1_p1",
      "description": "Subassembly trace row (step 1, column c=1; the five traced cells are value-identical, so cell 1 pins all of them): the datm stream values of datm_gswp3_streams.csv row (step 0, cell n=1) in as the Clmncep strm_* overrides (tbotmax, strm_tbot/strm_pbot/strm_wind/strm_shum/strm_lwdn/strm_swdn/strm_precn/strm_topo; strm_z = 1e30 spval, so the datamode falls back to Sa_z = 30 m), through the datm -> CLM chain (the Clmncep datamode laws of datm_datamode_clmncep_mod.F90: Sa_u = Sa_v = wind/sqrt(2), the Sa_shum clamp at qsat(tbotmax), the rain/snow split with frac = clamp((tbot - TKFRZ)*0.5, 0, 1) - all traced steps are ~249 K, far below freezing, so all precipitation falls as snow - and the Faxa_sw* direct/diffuse ratios; then the ImportFields import_fields + derive_quantities of lnd_import_export.F90:542-577 / lnd_import_export_utils.F90:66-90; then the Downscale copy + partition_precip path of atm2lndMod.F90:180-195, 359-390), out the CLM forcing rows of clm_bareground.csv (step 1, c=1; forc_t/forc_q/forc_pbot/forc_rho/forc_u/forc_v columns; forc_q pins the Sa_shum clamp law), clm_canopyflux.csv (step 1, stage=ent, c=1; forc_rain/forc_snow columns) and clm_surfrad.csv (step 1, c=1; forc_solad_vis/forc_solad_nir/forc_solai_vis/forc_solai_nir columns). The one-step offset is the CESM coupling sequence itself: the data atmosphere runs after the land within each coupling interval, so the land is forced by the previous interval's atmosphere (every forc_* dump value equals its one-step-earlier datm export bit-exact). The forc_t and forc_pbot assertions are pass-throughs of the stream values on this traced column and the forc_rain assertion pins the rain channel that is identically 0 on every traced step (all precipitation falls as snow): each is kept once per file as a labelled coupling-wiring check. The forc_wind and forc_solar assertions are derived (not a dump column): forc_wind = sqrt(forc_u^2 + forc_v^2) and forc_solar = forc_solad_vis + forc_solad_nir + forc_solai_vis + forc_solai_nir (equal to the datm strm_wind/strm_swdn stream columns through the datamode laws), computed and re-verified by stage1/analysis/extract_m9_test_rows.py.",
         "time_span": {
       "start": 0.0,
       "end": 0.0
      },
      "parameter_overrides": {
       "Clmncep.tbotmax": 310.35066065749163,
       "Clmncep.strm_tbot": 249.30924313863048,
